  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "In the diagram, $AB$ is parallel to $CD$. What is the value of $y$?",
  "image": "qimages/cemc/cayley-1998/q07.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "75"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "40"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "35"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "55"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "50"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Co-interior angles",
    "body": "Let the two lines meet $AB$ at $M$ and $CD$ at $N$ (left line) and $P$ (right line). Since $AB\\parallel CD$, the co-interior angles $\\angle BMN$ and $\\angle MND$ add to $180^\\circ$: $2x+70=180$, so $x=55$. In triangle $MNP$: $y=180-70-55=55$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 55**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Alternate angles",
    "body": "From $2x+70=180$ we get $x=55$. The angle $y^\\circ$ at $P$ and the angle $x^\\circ$ between $MP$ and $MB$ are alternate angles between the parallel lines, so $y=x=55$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 55**"
   }
  ],
