  },
  "grade": "10",
  "points": 6,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Rectangle $ABCD$ has length 9 and width 5. Diagonal $AC$ is divided into 5 equal parts at $W$, $X$, $Y$, and $Z$. Determine the area of the shaded region.",
  "image": "qimages/cemc/cayley-1998/q16.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "36"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$\\frac{36}{5}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "18"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$\\frac{4\\sqrt{106}}{5}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$\\frac{2\\sqrt{106}}{5}$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Equal small triangles",
    "body": "Triangle $ABC$ has area $\\frac12\\cdot9\\cdot5=\\frac{45}{2}$. The five triangles $ABW, WBX, XBY, YBZ, ZBC$ have equal bases on $AC$ and the same height from $B$, so each has area $\\frac{45}{2}\\div5=\\frac92$. The same holds for the five triangles with vertex $D$. The shaded region is made of four of these small triangles: $4\\cdot\\frac92=18$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 18**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Fraction of the rectangle",
    "body": "The ten small triangles (five on each side of $AC$) all have equal area and fill the rectangle of area $45$. Four of them are shaded, so the area is $\\frac4{10}\\cdot45=18$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 18**"
   }
  ],
