  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "If $N=\\left(7^{p+4}\\right)\\left(5^q\\right)\\left(2^3\\right)$ is a perfect cube, where $p$ and $q$ are positive integers, the smallest possible value of $p+q$ is",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "5"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "2"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "8"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "6"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "12"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Exponents divisible by 3",
    "body": "A number is a perfect cube exactly when every exponent in its prime factorization is a multiple of 3. So $p+4$ is a multiple of 3 (smallest positive $p$ is $2$) and $q$ is a multiple of 3 (smallest $q=3$). Smallest $p+q=5$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 5**"
   }
  ],
